Only the wasm32 build embeds it, because a browser has no system fonts.
Menus, tooltips, Help, disclosures and buttons draw these symbols from it.

Picker symbols font
===================

crates/model/fonts/ReShikiSymbols.ttf is a subset of DejaVu Sans 2.37 as
Ubuntu's fonts-dejavu-core 2.37-8 package installs it
(/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans.ttf, SHA-256
ae7b7855e115a5966d8b1b3f80f254ccc117ec86f9965e202ee2940453837280), holding
only the space and the symbol picker's symbols that Liberation Sans lacks:
⁺ ⁻ ↺ ↻ ⇄ ⇌ ⇒ ∝ ⊕ ⊖ ✓ ✗ ⟶. scripts/subset_symbols_font.py makes it the same
way as ReShiki Keys, and renames it ReShiki Symbols. Every build embeds it as
the last glyph fallback for measuring, drawing and export, so these symbols
draw where no installed font has them, as in the browser.
